Part 1 Reflection

There is no single “best” database. Organizations choose a DBMS based on their business requirements, such as
1- budget, 2- security needs, 3- scalability requirements, 4- existing technology ecosystem, 5- long-term strategy.

Oracle is often selected by large enterprises,
SQL Server by Microsoft-focused organizations,
PostgreSQL by startups and cloud-native companies,
MySQL by web application developers.

Each database has strengths and trade-offs that make it suitable for different environments

