Part 2 Reflection

Oracle is popular in large companies because it is secure, reliable, and can handle a large number of users and transactions.
Organizations such as banks, telecom companies, and government agencies use Oracle because their systems must run continuously without losing data.

Banks and telecom companies often choose Oracle because they process large amounts of important information every day.
Oracle provides strong security, backup, recovery, and high availability features that help keep their systems running safely.

Oracle is different from many traditional databases because it includes advanced enterprise features such as: (CDBs, PDBs, RAC, and Data Guard.)
These features make it easier to manage large systems, improve performance, and reduce downtime.

Oracle also offers different editions for different needs:
1-Oracle XE is free and mainly used for learning.
2-Standard Edition is suitable for small and medium businesses.
3-Enterprise Edition is designed for large organizations that need advanced features.

