Part 5 reflection

Most databases support the same basic features such as tables, relationships, joins, procedures, triggers, and transactions.
However, companies still choose different databases because they have different costs, performance levels, security features, and support options.

Companies may move from one database to another to save money, improve performance, move to the cloud, or support new business requirements.

Database migration can be difficult because data must be moved safely and applications may need changes to work with the new database.

Migration projects are considered risky because problems can cause data loss, system downtime, or business disruptions.

Database decisions are important because they affect a system’s performance, security, scalability, and future growth for many years.

Overall, companies choose the database that best fits their business needs, budget, and long-term goals.

